The legal text is the Revised Constitution of American Samoa, as published by the American Samoa Government at
https://www.americansamoa.gov/_files/ugd/4bfff9_637c7079564f4812ae2c848e48753e7d.pdf (a marked draft dated 6 September 2022
that shows the proposals of the 2022 Constitutional Convention in underline and strike-through).

The page that hosts the file states no reuse terms. The Constitution is an official legal text of the territory, ratified by the
United States Secretary of the Interior in 1967 and since amended by the Legislature, the voters and the Secretary. It is
republished here, unaltered except for the removal of the proposed (underlined) words, with credit to the American Samoa Government
as its publisher.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository is not legal advice
and not an official publication.
